1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
You didn't know already?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
I'm saying that
some of the humans are unique,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
by which I mean that they're practically
overflowing with life energy.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
We're calling them Rares
because they're quite difficult to find.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
[Turtle Ant] Difficult, you say?

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
[Rammot] What trick is this?

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
They seem to have gotten stronger
all of a sudden.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
[Killua] Thunderbolt!

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,000
[Rammot screams]

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
[Kite] If you wanna get stronger,
this is a perfect opportunity,

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
but if you aren't prepared,
you won't be able to endure the ordeal.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
From here on out,
in victory or defeat, it'll be hell.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
[opening theme music playing]

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
[singer singing in English]

17
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
KITE X AND X SLOTS

18
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
[narrator] Kite, Gon, and Killua
have advanced deep within the NGL

19
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
in search of the Chimera Ant nest,

20
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
and have now arrived at a cliff
with peculiar openings.

21
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Is this the place
where the Chimera Ants nest?

22
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,000
No, it's not.

23
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
so don't let your guard down.

24
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
The pill's called DD
and is mass-produced right here.

25
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
The hottest new drug on the mainland.

26
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
It's made from bira trees.
There must be a field close by.

27
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Ironic, given their status
as conservationists, right?

28
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
They're making more than just drugs. Look.

29
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
They're the same ones from earlier.

30
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
[Kite] If I had to hazard a guess,

31
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
I'd say only the leaders of the NGL
know the truth.

32
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
The other community members
probably genuinely identify

33
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
with the environmental message.

34
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
This facility, it's the core
of the NGL underground, isn't it?

35
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,000
and that a bunch of amateurs with guns
didn't stand a chance against them.

36
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
But what about their boss?

37
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:22,000
He either escaped or was eaten.
Either way this is bad news.

38
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
[Kite] They're slowly approaching
through the middle tunnel.

39
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
There are more in the left and right.

40
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,000
-Everything within 45 meters.
-[gasps] Did you say 45?

41
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Depending on my mental and physical state,
I'm able to increase that by a few meters.

42
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Here they come.

43
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
[scraping]

44
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
[whimpering]

45
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[both gasp]

46
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[men whimpering]

47
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Keep it down, you two.

48
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[men gagging]

49
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Hmm?

50
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Who the hell are you?

51
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
How dare you intrude on my turf?

52
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Help us. You gotta help us.

53
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Shut your damn mouth, Spot.

54
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
You're a dog, remember?

55
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
[gasps]

56
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[chuckling] Oops.
I didn't mean to do that.

57
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[man whimpers]

58
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,000
[panting]

59
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
No, don't!

60
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
-Let me go.
-Don't move carelessly.

61
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:25,000
There's more than one enemy here,
and they want you to rush toward them.

62
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
[boys gasp]

63
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[laughing]

64
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Now, bye-bye.

65
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
[whimpers]

66
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Help me.

67
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
They've always been aggressive,

68
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:15,000
but consuming malicious humans
has had an effect on them,

69
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
and it's made them even more evil.

70
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Huh? What do you mean?

71
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Phagogenesis, right?

72
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
If we don't deal with them here,

73
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
there's no telling
how many more people will be killed.

74
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Go, capture them.

75
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
I'll take the one in the back.

76
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
The ones rushing at us will go to you two.

77
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Okay, we got it.

78
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
[Kite] Don't hesitate. Fight to kill.

79
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
[boys] Bring it!

80
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
-[grunting]
-[screeching]

81
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
[cackling]

82
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Now, this next one is just for you.
My unblockable thousand-hand fist.

83
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
[shouts]

84
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,000
[screams]

85
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
Hmm. That sure was a close one.

86
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
You have a lot more power
than I was expecting.

87
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
[Gon] Damn, these guys are tough.

88
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:47,000
They have the hard shells of insects,
combined with the agility of humans.

89
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Hmm, I wonder what's running
through your mind right now.

90
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
-[Gon] He's right.
-Huh?

91
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
I can't hesitate.

92
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Now, show me rock!

93
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[Killua] Don't hesitate, kill.

94
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[laughing]

95
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
[Killua] Been a while
since I flipped my switch on.

96
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[Mosquito Ant screeches]

97
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
SERPENT WORK

98
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
You!

99
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:55,000
[laughs] You pathetic little fool.
This is my real stinger.

100
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
[groans softly]

101
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Well, how does it feel as the poison
spreads through your body? Feel good?

102
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Hmm, works like a charm.

103
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Once I get him addicted,
we'll have another human dog.

104
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Are you done over there?

105
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Oh, guess not.

106
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
[neck cracks]

107
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
But how?

108
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Yeah. Poison doesn't work on me, sorry.

109
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Oh, I see.

110
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,000
-If you behave, I'll make this quick.
-Oh, well.

111
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
[body thudding]

112
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[scoffs] Can't believe
she fell for a cheap trick.

113
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,000
[Centipede] What is this power
overflowing from his body?

114
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Any closer,
and I could get seriously injured, but…

115
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
The source of his power is in his fist.

116
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Or maybe he'll pull his punch
and use a kick.

117
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,000
No, he's definitely going to use his fist.

118
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
then I can bite him and inject my venom.

119
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Let's run a little simulation.

120
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[grunts]

121
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[yelling]

122
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
[Centipede] Yes, it'll work.

123
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
It's just a punch.

124
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:54,000
No matter how strong it is,
I can take it as long as I'm prepared.

125
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
[Yunju] Hey, we should
get this started soon, huh?

126
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,000
-Wait a little longer.
-Screw that!

127
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
It's not like you have a choice anyway.

128
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[sighs]

129
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Now, let me see what you've got.

130
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
If you insist.

131
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[Yunju] Huh? This is my castle.

132
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
A king doesn't need to have a reason
to be in his own castle.

133
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
I would expect
you'd want to avoid this place.

134
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,000
-Huh?
-He should be here.

135
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Beats me. I figure he's probably
already inside the queen's belly.

136
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,000
who likes to amuse himself
by making humans into dogs.

137
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
[laughs] Is that so?

138
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Well, you're right,
I can't wait to strip you down,

139
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
and put a collar around your neck.

140
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[grunts]

141
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Bastard.

142
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
[growls]

143
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
[Yunju yells]

144
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[grunts, groans]

145
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Damn it! [grunts]

146
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[Crazy Slots] You know what
your problem is? You're too impatient.

147
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[mimics whirring]

148
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Are you messing with me?

149
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Forget about making you my dog,
I'm going to kill you.

150
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:18,000
-Four.
-Really? That's a bad spin.

151
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
What did you just say?

152
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
I don't have any bad spins,
ungrateful bastard.

153
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
You're dead!

154
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[thudding]

155
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
[grunting]

156
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[Centipede] I'm gonna pretend
to attack him while I block his punch,

157
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:57,000
and then, when his guard is down,
I'll just grab him up and take a bite.

158
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Here goes.

159
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
[yelling]

160
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Janken…

161
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[Centipede] Just like I thought. Block!

162
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Impossible! Where the hell
was he hiding that thing?

163
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
[Kite] Don't relax,
even after dismembering them.

164
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,000
You have to stay vigilant.

165
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Remember, the head and body
can survive for an entire day

166
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
after they've been separated.

167
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
No matter what, destroy the head.

168
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:21,000
And whenever you kill one, if you can,
make sure you do it quietly and quickly.

169
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[cackling]

170
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:37,000
I'm the great mad clown
known as Crazy Slots.

171
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Don't ever forget that, okay?

172
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
-[Kite] Just leave already.
-[Crazy Slots gasps]

173
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,000
[Killua] What a weird power.

174
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
-So it talks on its own?
-Pretty much.

175
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Since it's a roulette wheel,

176
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
does that mean you don't get to choose
what weapon you get?

177
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Right.

178
00:18:55,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Sadly, once I get one, I'm not allowed to
exchange it for another, no matter what.

179
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
I'm stuck. [sighs]

180
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[wing blowing]

181
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:21,000
It appears that we've lost the signal
from Yunju's team.

182
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
[Leol] Were they killed?

183
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
The signal indicated three enemies,

184
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
and that they looked tastier
than the others.

185
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,000
So tasty that I just can't believe it.
Yum-yum. [slurps]

186
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:38,000
[Leol] So they must be
the Rares. [chuckles]

187
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Now we have a reason to go.

188
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Yunju was using the factory as his base?

189
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:48,000
[Flutter] He was, so I'm sure the rare
humans will still be near the facility.

190
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Oh, yay! I love feasts.

191
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:01,000
[Kite] As you saw, both of your powers
are significantly easier to use than mine.

192
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
You're not kidding.
Anything's easier than that.

193
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Yeah.

194
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:12,000
[Kite] Gon, you seem to have incorporated
enhancer, transmuter and emitter abilities

195
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
into your rock, paper, scissors.

196
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:33,000
You'll have ample opportunity to improve.
Let's hurry, the nest is close.

197
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
I don't know what's happening, but…

198
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[breathing heavily]

199
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,000
[laughs]

200
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:09,000
My body, it's overflowing with energy.

201
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
What in the hell is all this, huh?

202
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
[Peggy] What's the matter, Colt?

203
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:22,000
A signal from a soldier.
Rammot is acting strangely.

204
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
[Peggy] In what way?

205
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
I've never witnessed
such ferocious life energy.

206
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
[continues laughing]

207
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

208
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[upbeat music playing]

209
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Gon] Next time, "Inspiration To Evolve".

210
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
I want inspiration to evolve.

211
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,000
[Killua] Okay, but when will you?

212
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[Gon and Killua] Now, of course.
